{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310523,"nonce":"2qAbukhjhc+IIKm389YwGKJOn/E=","title":"FIXED — Anon-struct field scramble had two compounding causes. Both fixed. Real Llama-3-8B GGUF metadata now reads correctly through ...","message":"`nue.loader.GGUFLoader.readMetadata(path)` returned a 13-field `ModelMetadata` typedef with scrambled Int/Float values — most fields off by one slot, garbage in Float slots. String (`architecture`) and Bool (`tieWordEmbeddings`) fields correct.\n\n\nThe RD (recursive descent) parser at `parse_anonymous_type` ([parser/src/rd/types.rs:206](parser/src/rd/types.rs#L206)) did not handle field-level metadata. When it saw `@:optional var b:Int` in a typedef body, the field-loop:\n1. Tried to eat `KwVar` / `KwFinal` / `?` — all failed (current token = `AtColon`).\n2. Took `AtColon`'s text (`@:`) as the field name and advanced.\n3. `expect(Colon)` failed → `parse_anonymous_type` returned `Err`.\n\nThe error bubbled up through `parse_typedef` → `parse_type_declaration` → `parse_file`, which captured it in `self.errors` and returned `Err(errors)`. Then `parse_haxe_file_with_config` ([parser/src/haxe_parser.rs:88-94](parser/src/haxe_parser.rs#L88)) silently discarded `_rd_errors` and fell back to the legacy nom parser. The nom path, in turn, got confused by `1e-5` in some adjacent literal and silently dropped the surrounding class declaration — surfacing as SIGILL at unrelated call sites or scrambled-value bugs.\n\n\nEven if the parser succeeded, `lower_object_literal` ([compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs:32395](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L32395)) was computing slot indices from the literal's own narrow inferred type, while field readers computed slots from the full typedef's alphabetically-sorted field list. Off-by-one for every field after the missing `@:optional`'s alphabetical position.\n\n\n**Parser** ([parser/src/rd/types.rs:206](parser/src/rd/types.rs#L206)) — `parse_anonymous_type` field loop now calls `parse_metadata_list()` first and ORs `optional_from_meta` (`@:optional`) with `optional_from_question` (`?` shorthand). RD no longer errors on the canonical Haxe optional spelling, so the silent nom fallback is never triggered.\n\n**MIR** ([compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs:99](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L99)) — added `HirToMirContext::object_literal_target_ty: Option\u003cTypeId\u003e` hint, set by `HirStatement::Return` (function's return type), `Let` (type_hint), and `Assign` (lhs symbol's type_id). `lower_object_literal` uses `target_ty.unwrap_or(expr_type)` so the writer's slot table matches what readers compute over the typedef shape (including optional defaults).\n\n\n```\n$ rayzor run /tmp/anon_cross/Main.hx\narch     = llama\nhidden   = 4096\ninter    = 14336\nlayers   = 32\nheads    = 32\nkv_heads = 8\nheadDim  = 128\nvocab    = 128256\nseq      = 8192\nnorm     = 0.00001\nrope     = 500000\ntie      = false\n```\n\nAnd against the real Llama-3-8B GGUF (`Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf`) via `nue.loader.GGUFLoader.readMetadata` — all 12 fields read correctly. 128/128 haxe regression passes.\n\n\nThe fixes are general: any typedef with `@:optional` fields where the literal omits them now round-trips correctly across Return / Let / Assign and cross-module boundaries.\n\nThe silent RD→nom fallback at [parser/src/haxe_parser.rs:88-94](parser/src/haxe_parser.rs#L88) now surfaces every RD failure to stderr (deduped by `(file, offset, message)`, since stdlib files get re-parsed many times). With the warning visible, the next RD bug to hide a real issue will be noticeable instead of weeks of debugging.\n\nSubsequently fixed RD gaps so the fallback is rarely hit:\n\n- import.hx leniency (typedef/class/interface allowed)\n- Recursive preprocessor for nested `#if` inside selected branches\n- Inline `#if ... #end` on the same line counts toward depth in `extract_conditional_block`\n- Function-typed fields in anon types (`{ function iterator():Iterator\u003cT\u003e }`)\n- `final name:T` class fields where `final` is consumed as a Modifier first\n- Property with initialiser (`var X(default, null) = ...`) — downgrades to Var\n- `.code` postfix on case-pattern literals (`case '\u0026'.code:`)\n- Expression-level metadata (`@:privateAccess obj.field`)\n- Trailing-dot float literals (`4503599627370496.`)\n- Zero-arg compiler intrinsics (`__resources__()`)\n\nOnly remaining fallback: `haxe/Int64.hx` uses multi-var declarations (`var a = 1, b = 2;`). Implementing the splice in `parse_block_expr` works AS PARSING, but it shifts the parsed AST for StringTools (which also uses multi-var) and exposes a BLADE caching fragility — when `test_file_readall` caches StringTools via the new RD path and then `test_stringbuf_stringtools` loads from cache, the cached function-ID map doesn't line up and we get SIGILL. Documented as: fix needs a BLADE invariance pass (or to make sure RD and nom produce identical MIR for the same source), not a parser-only change.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_anon_field_scramble` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}